# Services kept off.
# System Settings → Keyboard → Keyboard Shortcuts → Services.
#
# One pbs NSServicesStatus key per line. Text after # is a note.
# Blank lines and lines beginning with # are ignored.
#
# macos.sh merges each key into NSServicesStatus (it does not replace the
# dictionary). A key is off when enabled_context_menu, enabled_services_menu,
# and presentation_modes ContextMenu and ServicesMenu are 0 or false.
# A missing key is written. A key that is already off is left alone.
# Stickies had only enabled_services_menu saved; the pin sets both menus off.
#
# These three are unticked in System Settings and have no saved entry, because
# they are off by default. Do not add them:
#   New CotEditor Window Containing Selection
#   New TextEdit Window Containing Selection
#   Summarise

com.apple.Safari - Add to Reading List - addToReadingList
com.apple.ChineseTextConverterService - Convert Text from Simplified to Traditional Chinese - convertTextToTraditionalChinese
com.apple.ChineseTextConverterService - Convert Text from Traditional to Simplified Chinese - convertTextToSimplifiedChinese
com.apple.Stickies - Make Sticky - makeStickyFromTextService
com.apple.Terminal - Open man Page in Terminal - openManPage
com.apple.Terminal - Search man Page Index in Terminal - searchManPages
com.apple.services.addToiTunesAsSpokenTrack - Add to Music as a Spoken Track - runWorkflowAsService
com.apple.services.showMap - Show Map - runWorkflowAsService
org.hammerspoon.Hammerspoon - Send to Hammerspoon - processDockIconDraggedText
